WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.470
When the Queen's parade reached the croquet lawn, Alice heard a soft voice beside her.

2
00:00:07.471 --> 00:00:11.603
"It's . . . it's a fine day," the White Rabbit said.

3
00:00:11.604 --> 00:00:14.356
He looked anxiously at Alice.

4
00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:18.820
"Very fine indeed," Alice replied. "Where's the Duchess?"

5
00:00:18.821 --> 00:00:22.263
"Be quiet!" the White Rabbit said quickly.

6
00:00:22.264 --> 00:00:26.234
He looked over his shoulder before whispering in Alice's ear.

7
00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:30.292
"The Duchess has been sentenced to death."

8
00:00:30.293 --> 00:00:35.103
Alice looked surprised. "What did she do?"

9
00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:40.260
"She slapped the Queen's face, and—" the White Rabbit began.

10
00:00:40.261 --> 00:00:44.053
Alice laughed nervously.

11
00:00:44.054 --> 00:00:51.030
"Oh, hush, before the Queen hears you!" the White Rabbit said, sounding frightened.

12
00:00:51.031 --> 00:00:55.163
"The Duchess arrived late, and—"

13
00:00:55.164 --> 00:00:59.841
"Go to your places!" the Queen roared.

14
00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:04.679
People began running in all directions, tripping over each other.

15
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:10.757
However, they soon settled down, and the croquet game began.

16
00:01:10.758 --> 00:01:15.915
"This is the strangest croquet game I've ever seen," Alice said.

17
00:01:15.916 --> 00:01:20.360
"The balls are live hedgehogs, and the mallets are flamingos.

18
00:01:20.361 --> 00:01:24.486
And what are those soldiers doing?"

19
00:01:24.487 --> 00:01:29.247
The soldiers were bending over so their hands touched the ground.

20
00:01:29.248 --> 00:01:37.197
"Oh, I see! They're the wickets!" Alice exclaimed.

21
00:01:37.198 --> 00:01:39.653
She picked up her flamingo.

22
00:01:39.654 --> 00:01:43.388
But her flamingo wouldn't cooperate.

23
00:01:43.389 --> 00:01:48.138
Alice couldn't figure out how to hold it as a mallet.

24
00:01:48.139 --> 00:01:54.826
The bird kept looking at her with a puzzled expression, which only made Alice laugh.

25
00:01:54.827 --> 00:02:04.017
As for her hedgehog, it unrolled itself and began to walk away.

26
00:02:04.018 --> 00:02:07.606
The soldiers kept getting up to stretch.

27
00:02:07.607 --> 00:02:13.382
And the ground was too rough to play on.

28
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:18.082
"This is a hard way to play croquet," Alice said.

29
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:20.338
The players didn't take turns.

30
00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:27.253
Instead they all made their shots at once, which led to many arguments.

31
00:02:27.254 --> 00:02:34.289
Soon the Queen was stomping around, shouting, "Off with his head! Off with her head!"

32
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.375
Alice began to feel uneasy.

33
00:02:37.376 --> 00:02:41.564
"I hope I don't do anything to upset the Queen," she thought.

34
00:02:41.565 --> 00:02:43.976
"That could be dangerous."

35
00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:50.282
Suddenly she saw something odd floating in the air—a grin.

36
00:02:50.283 --> 00:02:56.681
The image grew clearer. "It's the Cheshire Cat!" Alice said happily.

37
00:02:56.682 --> 00:02:59.797
"Now I'll have somebody to talk to."

38
00:02:59.798 --> 00:03:06.888
"How are you doing?" the Cheshire Cat asked.

39
00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:11.716
"There's no use replying until his ears show up," Alice said to herself.

40
00:03:11.717 --> 00:03:13.701
"He can't hear me yet."

41
00:03:13.702 --> 00:03:18.071
In another minute the Cheshire Cat's whole head was visible.

42
00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:23.010
Alice put down her flamingo and began to describe the croquet game.

43
00:03:23.011 --> 00:03:27.578
Meanwhile the Cheshire Cat's body remained invisible.

44
00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:31.599
"Nobody plays fairly," Alice complained.

45
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:38.865
"And it's so difficult using live animals and soldiers."

46
00:03:38.866 --> 00:03:45.845
"How do you like the Queen?" the Cheshire Cat asked quietly.

47
00:03:45.846 --> 00:03:48.937
"I don't like her at all," Alice said.

48
00:03:48.938 --> 00:03:55.183
"She's so—" Just then Alice noticed the Queen listening nearby.

49
00:03:55.184 --> 00:04:03.591
She blushed. "I mean, the Queen is likely to win, so it's not worth finishing the game."

50
00:04:03.592 --> 00:04:08.131
The Queen smiled and passed by.

51
00:04:08.132 --> 00:04:16.837
As Alice continued to talk, the King approached and stared at the Cheshire Cat's head.

52
00:04:16.838 --> 00:04:22.140
"Who are you talking to?" the King asked Alice.

53
00:04:22.141 --> 00:04:26.300
"This is a good friend of mine, the Cheshire Cat," she said.

54
00:04:26.301 --> 00:04:28.423
"Let me introduce you."

55
00:04:28.424 --> 00:04:32.525
"I don't like the look of that cat at all.

56
00:04:32.526 --> 00:04:37.018
He must be removed at once."

57
00:04:37.019 --> 00:04:39.475
The King called out to the Queen.

58
00:04:39.476 --> 00:04:45.068
"My dear! Please have this cat removed!"

59
00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:50.385
The Queen had only one way of dealing with problems, large or small.

60
00:04:50.386 --> 00:04:53.852
"Off with his head!" she cried.

61
00:04:53.853 --> 00:04:59.005
The King went to fetch the Executioner.

